  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed roof terrace, by reason of its siting, size, and elevated relationship with neighbouring properties, would enable direct and prolonged overlooking into adjoining rear gardens and rear-facing habitable rooms. This would result in an unacceptable level of actual and perceived overlooking, leading to undue loss of privacy and increased noise and disturbance for neighbouring occupiers. The development constitutes an unneighbourly form of development and is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D4 of the London Plan (2021), Policies DMD 8 and DMD 68 of the Development Management Document (2014), and Core Strategy Policy 30 (2010).",
    "The proposed roof terrace, including the associated glazed screening, by virtue of its design, materials, scale, siting, and projection, would represent an awkward and incongruous addition that fails to relate to the architectural style of the host dwelling and disrupts the established character, form, and pattern of development along Station Road. The proposal is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), Policies DMD8 and DMD 37 of the Development Management Document (2014), and Core Strategy Policy 30 (2010)."
  ],
